WEBVTT

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Class 3-2</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Hirose Natsuko</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Virtuoso</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:00.020 --> 00:03.230
<b>Early Spring</b>

00:01.430 --> 00:05.730
What kind of story is <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>?

00:05.730 --> 00:09.730
In <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, 
there are nine countries...

00:10.210 --> 00:14.730
and each of them has this thing that 
shines like the sun called a Soul Future.

00:15.860 --> 00:20.610
Everyone's able to live happy, fun lives
 because of the Soul Futures.

00:21.670 --> 00:26.330
But suddenly, the Voids arrive
and start eating the Soul Futures! Wah!

00:26.330 --> 00:30.640
And if the Voids eat all nine Soul Futures,

00:31.310 --> 00:35.340
the Great Void that spells
the end of the world appears!

00:35.340 --> 00:36.490
Isn't that crazy?

00:37.050 --> 00:42.630
So, yeah. That's why the best warriors come 
together to stop the Great Void from forming.

00:42.630 --> 00:46.310
Nine of them! The Nine Soldiers!

00:47.500 --> 00:51.200
The Nine Soldiers fight their 
hardest to save the world.

00:51.200 --> 00:52.740
But Luke...

00:53.250 --> 00:55.690
Um, Luke...

00:59.140 --> 01:01.990
Luke!

01:08.220 --> 01:10.810
Huh? I...

02:42.550 --> 02:47.980
Episode 2: Defending to the Death.

02:49.540 --> 02:51.150
Isn't this...

02:53.300 --> 02:54.770
Hirose Natsuko.

02:55.110 --> 02:58.770
Where is this country called Real World?
 Was that a summoning spell you used?

02:58.770 --> 03:00.660
Are anneemators wizards?

03:00.660 --> 03:02.280
H-H-Hold on a sec.

03:02.280 --> 03:03.650
Just who are you?

03:08.370 --> 03:10.090
I'm hungry.

03:15.310 --> 03:17.930
I was asleep for three days?

03:17.930 --> 03:20.500
No wonder I'm starving.

03:21.060 --> 03:21.900
Eat.

03:23.940 --> 03:25.310
Thanks for the food.

03:37.310 --> 03:38.320
It's so good!

03:44.640 --> 03:48.750
It didn't say anything about Luke being able 
to cook in his character reference sheets.

03:48.750 --> 03:53.090
"Reference sheets"? What are they? 
What's written about me?

03:53.090 --> 03:57.470
Oh, they have like the backgrounds for the town 
and stuff about the Nine Soldiers.

03:57.770 --> 03:59.330
I'm included in there?

03:59.810 --> 04:02.760
Luke Braveheart. 
Comes from the Country of Heroes.

04:02.760 --> 04:05.470
Legendary hero. 
Equipped with the King Brave Sword.

04:05.470 --> 04:09.960
Height: 175 cm. Weight: 62 kg. 
First-person pronoun: "Ore."

04:09.960 --> 04:12.610
Dislikes: groups of young women.

04:12.610 --> 04:15.640
I-I do <i>not</i> dislike groups of young women!

04:15.640 --> 04:18.410
What are these "whatever sheets"
 you speak of? Show them to me!

04:18.410 --> 04:19.350
I didn't bring 'em.

04:20.770 --> 04:23.570
What do you plan to do 
with all this information?

04:23.570 --> 04:24.580
Hm...

04:25.040 --> 04:25.880
Observe?

04:25.880 --> 04:27.230
Why observe?

04:28.240 --> 04:29.370
For enjoyment?

04:29.370 --> 04:30.470
Are you a pervert?

04:32.410 --> 04:33.620
Is there more?

04:33.620 --> 04:35.340
This is super good!

04:37.750 --> 04:39.960
Man, I'm stuffed.

04:40.390 --> 04:43.800
So where did that strange 
white table come from?

04:43.800 --> 04:47.080
Oh, my animation desk? 
I was pretty shocked about that, too.

04:47.350 --> 04:48.610
What is that?

04:48.610 --> 04:50.100
Just watch.

04:50.100 --> 04:53.160
Come forth! I'll draw anything for you!

04:56.610 --> 04:59.450
Hirose Natsuko's gonna draw!

05:02.990 --> 05:05.720
Hey, do that thing you did last time, thanks.

05:10.870 --> 05:12.570
Uh, hello? Start shining!

05:12.570 --> 05:14.890
Summon the animation desk,
or I'll snap you in two!

05:17.030 --> 05:19.280
But yeah, last time, my pegbar was all like,

05:19.280 --> 05:22.330
"Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko," 
and started talking to me.

05:22.610 --> 05:25.280
It started shining, 
the animation desk came out,

05:25.280 --> 05:27.080
then the thing I drew appeared like "bam"!

05:27.080 --> 05:28.090
And then, uh, I...

05:28.430 --> 05:30.070
So this is the source of your power?

05:30.070 --> 05:31.910
Hey, wait. Give that back.

05:31.910 --> 05:33.130
I don't sense anything.

05:33.130 --> 05:33.850
Give it back.

05:45.090 --> 05:46.700
Mornin'.

05:47.270 --> 05:50.840
D-D-Don't eat Luke, you crazy monster!

05:50.840 --> 05:52.530
Begone, black-haired gremlin!

05:53.030 --> 05:56.250
Who do you think kept you alive, huh? Well?

05:56.250 --> 05:57.330
Stop that!

05:57.620 --> 06:01.230
I'm one of the Nine Soldiers! 
You should respect me more!

06:01.230 --> 06:04.660
Do you have any idea how much money
I spent trying to get your acrylic key chain?

06:04.660 --> 06:07.810
You need to respect the fans 
that drop money on you more.

06:07.810 --> 06:11.150
Wh-What are you even talking about?

06:11.150 --> 06:14.260
Oh, Natsuko-san. You're awake.

06:14.530 --> 06:16.600
I'm glad you seem well.

06:16.600 --> 06:19.720
Memerun! This black-haired 
gremlin's being mean to me!

06:19.720 --> 06:21.070
Heal me!

06:21.070 --> 06:22.390
I refuse.

06:22.390 --> 06:25.080
Everyone, the mayor is calling for us.

06:25.730 --> 06:27.850
Wonder if it's to reward us 
for beating the Voids.

06:27.850 --> 06:29.770
I'm not done questioning you.

06:29.770 --> 06:31.860
Stay here until we're done.

06:31.860 --> 06:37.330
Actually, he requested Hirose Natsuko
accompany us if she had awakened.

06:39.880 --> 06:41.370
Huh?

06:41.370 --> 06:42.870
Are you serious right now?

06:42.870 --> 06:45.140
Seeing the mayor of the Last City up close,

06:45.140 --> 06:48.940
his clothing's lack of 
coverage is actually insane.

06:48.940 --> 06:51.120
It's even more intense in person.

06:51.120 --> 06:53.080
He's so ripped!

06:51.490 --> 06:53.400
Hey, you're being rude!

06:55.730 --> 06:56.900
That voice!

06:57.150 --> 06:59.640
The prophet, Baobab-sama!

07:00.500 --> 07:01.890
Look at this form!

07:01.890 --> 07:04.360
The hair style! The color! 
The character design is perfect!

07:03.350 --> 07:07.660
I'm so sorry about that thing!
It's kinda insane!

07:04.360 --> 07:07.660
Wow, so that's what you 
look like behind the ears.

07:10.110 --> 07:14.400
I'm glad to see there's still 
such a lively lass left in this world.

07:14.400 --> 07:16.620
A lass? That's a girl?

07:16.620 --> 07:18.910
Do you have a face?

07:19.400 --> 07:21.910
Ah, so you're human.

07:21.910 --> 07:25.500
Hirose Natsuko. Where is 
this country called the Real World?

07:25.500 --> 07:27.660
That's what I'd like to know.

07:27.660 --> 07:29.720
How did you get to this city?

07:30.140 --> 07:35.270
I think I ate a rotten clam lunch, died...

07:35.850 --> 07:38.590
and somehow ended up in this anime's world.

07:38.590 --> 07:39.860
"Anime"?

07:39.860 --> 07:41.000
Allow me to explain!

07:41.000 --> 07:46.550
This is the world in an anime film 
created by director, Tsuruyama Kametaro!

07:46.550 --> 07:49.800
One second is 24 FPS 
and if we animate in threes,

07:49.800 --> 07:51.900
that's eight drawings per second.

07:51.900 --> 07:55.300
All of you are drawings,
drawn by... animators!

07:59.150 --> 08:02.860
Wait. Why was I reincarnated 
into <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>, though?

08:03.560 --> 08:07.020
And I'm still me, so maybe I just 
teleported here rather than reincarnated?

08:06.020 --> 08:11.820
Yikes. She's so crazy, 
she's <i>beyond</i> out there.

08:07.020 --> 08:09.700
So wait, did I die? Or am I alive?

08:09.700 --> 08:12.160
I'm pretty sure I died back there.

08:12.390 --> 08:13.840
Sir, what did you need?

08:14.330 --> 08:15.420
Baobab-sama.

08:15.660 --> 08:16.450
Right.

08:16.840 --> 08:20.380
It's common for things beyond human 
understanding to happen in our world.

08:20.380 --> 08:23.880
There is only one Soul Future left.

08:24.930 --> 08:29.330
As all of you know, once all 
of the Soul Futures are gone,

08:29.330 --> 08:33.320
the Great Void will appear, 
and this world will end.

08:33.880 --> 08:42.460
What we must do right now is stop 
the Great Void from appearing at all costs.

08:44.480 --> 08:49.170
I believe we should recruit 
Hirose Natsuko into the Nine Soldiers.

08:49.440 --> 08:50.120
Huh?

08:50.660 --> 08:52.160
What?!

08:52.160 --> 08:57.460
I believe this girl has what it takes to be
 one of the Nine Soldiers. What do you think?

08:57.460 --> 08:58.720
Absolutely not!

08:58.720 --> 09:02.890
I do not want this inexplicable, black-haired 
heathen assuming the Nine Soldiers mantle!

09:02.890 --> 09:03.980
Oh?

09:04.630 --> 09:07.350
Um, well... I mean...

09:07.350 --> 09:11.190
You know how it is. 
The Nine Soldiers doesn't need a woman.

09:11.190 --> 09:12.060
What?

09:12.060 --> 09:15.060
Women are quick to cry, they're weak,

09:15.060 --> 09:17.350
and they gossip when they're in groups.

09:17.350 --> 09:18.590
She'll hold us back.

09:18.590 --> 09:19.780
Memerun's right there.

09:20.080 --> 09:21.790
Well, Memerun's...

09:22.320 --> 09:23.540
a warrior.

09:23.540 --> 09:25.550
Well, you heard him, Memerun.

09:27.350 --> 09:29.170
Memerun's allowed to be with us.

09:29.170 --> 09:31.090
Whereas you aren't!

09:31.090 --> 09:34.040
I absolutely refuse to let you
 join the Nine Soldiers.

09:34.280 --> 09:36.060
I don't want to be one, anyway.

09:36.060 --> 09:39.600
Soon after this, Voids fall from the sky
 and it's gonna be a huge ordeal,

09:39.600 --> 09:42.360
so I'd just die again 
if I became one of the Nine Soldiers.

09:42.360 --> 09:44.330
Voids from the sky?

09:44.330 --> 09:46.440
There's no way Voids can fly.

09:46.440 --> 09:47.490
Right, QJ?

09:47.490 --> 09:49.780
The chances are low, but...

09:49.780 --> 09:52.550
Quit saying random things. Explain yourself.

09:53.050 --> 09:53.960
Hey!

09:53.960 --> 09:58.270
Well, all women do is gossip and 
hold you back, so I'm just not gonna talk.

09:58.270 --> 09:59.620
Now you listen here...

09:59.620 --> 10:00.920
What?

10:04.310 --> 10:06.030
Aw, man.

10:06.030 --> 10:09.800
And I totally thought 
we were gonna get a reward.

10:09.800 --> 10:11.140
Where's that woman?

10:11.140 --> 10:14.250
She ran that way in quite a hurry.

10:14.250 --> 10:15.420
Where did she go?

10:15.420 --> 10:16.570
I'm unsure.

10:16.940 --> 10:20.680
Yay! She's finally gone!

10:19.600 --> 10:20.680
Memerun...

10:20.680 --> 10:23.180
About earlier... I'm sorry.

10:23.180 --> 10:27.030
Memerun, wanna ride on my back?

10:27.030 --> 10:28.200
That's quite all right.

10:32.440 --> 10:33.490
Yeah, nope.

10:33.490 --> 10:34.820
Nope, nope, nope, nope.

10:35.090 --> 10:37.940
I can't stay in this world.
I'm going back to the real world.

10:40.120 --> 10:41.950
I think it was somewhere around here.

10:43.070 --> 10:45.220
Lord, I beseech thee.

10:45.220 --> 10:47.520
Please return me to my former world.

10:47.520 --> 10:51.590
I don't want to hate 
my beloved <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>.

10:51.890 --> 10:54.840
If you let me go back to 
the real world, I'll do anything.

10:54.840 --> 10:56.450
I'll never ask for anything again.

10:56.450 --> 10:58.840
Please bring me back to life!

11:12.130 --> 11:14.860
Don't wanna, don't wanna, 
don't wanna, don't wanna be here!

11:14.860 --> 11:18.320
Wanna go home, 
wanna go home, wanna go home!

11:27.770 --> 11:31.560
Man, I knew I should've watched 
more series with reincarnation in them.

11:31.560 --> 11:33.910
How the heck will I get back
 to the real world?

11:45.720 --> 11:47.960
And that's my 100th victory in a row.

11:48.460 --> 11:51.720
One more time! Let's play one more time!

12:00.910 --> 12:02.680
So good!

12:03.100 --> 12:06.110
You didn't have to let her in.

12:06.640 --> 12:09.040
You said the Voids were 
going to come from the sky.

12:10.030 --> 12:11.660
You believe her?

12:11.660 --> 12:15.530
Hirose Natsuko knew about that
previous army of Voids coming here.

12:15.910 --> 12:19.480
Apparently, the country of the 
Real World has these "whatever sheets,"

12:19.480 --> 12:21.790
and it's all written on there in detail.

12:21.790 --> 12:23.550
Huh? What the heck?

12:23.860 --> 12:25.640
How will they come from the sky?

12:27.070 --> 12:28.930
Got something I can draw with?

12:32.170 --> 12:34.560
Whoa.

12:34.890 --> 12:36.330
This is the mothership.

12:36.330 --> 12:39.830
Countless flying Voids are 
going to come out of here.

12:40.190 --> 12:41.410
You...

12:41.810 --> 12:44.830
are <i>really</i> good at drawing!

12:44.830 --> 12:46.330
It's what pays the bills.

12:47.100 --> 12:48.300
What do you think?

12:48.900 --> 12:51.230
I haven't seen this type before.

12:51.250 --> 12:54.670
The probability they will come down
from the sky is not zero, but...

12:56.610 --> 12:59.450
These Voids will show up 
during the harvest festival.

12:59.450 --> 13:00.830
That's in three days.

13:01.210 --> 13:04.330
A lot of the crops are 
devastatingly destroyed,

13:04.330 --> 13:08.380
causing a severe food shortage 
for the Last City, and many die.

13:08.680 --> 13:11.090
Don't say scary things like that.

13:12.700 --> 13:14.600
What's your goal?

13:14.600 --> 13:16.620
Why did you come back here?

13:17.870 --> 13:21.850
I want to go back to the real world, 
but I don't know how to get there.

13:22.260 --> 13:24.850
If I'm gonna have to live 
in this world for a while,

13:25.230 --> 13:27.650
there's something I have 
to protect, no matter what.

13:29.540 --> 13:30.880
What will you protect?

13:33.460 --> 13:34.600
Well...

13:36.440 --> 13:37.600
Food!

13:39.580 --> 13:42.330
Every day until I'm brought back to life...

13:43.610 --> 13:46.150
I'm gonna eat food!

13:48.490 --> 13:49.500
Delicious!

13:49.900 --> 13:52.420
What the heck is she talking about?

13:53.210 --> 13:57.650
Can you not use your anneemator 
summoning magic like you did last time?

13:58.040 --> 14:03.000
Nope. My pegbar's not talking to me anymore,
 so there's no guarantee I can do it again.

14:03.000 --> 14:05.020
But I will join the Nine Soldiers.

14:05.020 --> 14:07.450
Didn't you say you were going to decline?

14:07.450 --> 14:09.870
I recalled that, according 
to the reference sheets,

14:09.870 --> 14:13.020
the Nine Soldiers can eat and drink 
all they want at the tavern next door.

14:13.020 --> 14:14.700
Talk about low aspirations!

14:14.700 --> 14:17.430
She could never be one of the Nine Soldiers.

14:17.430 --> 14:20.290
Don't go underestimating 
the Nine Soldiers. Right, Luke?

14:20.290 --> 14:21.480
I have one condition.

14:21.480 --> 14:22.260
Huh?

14:22.260 --> 14:27.380
If the Voids show up three days from now
 like you say, and we're able to defeat them...

14:27.790 --> 14:30.220
I'll officially agree to you 
joining the Nine Soldiers.

14:34.000 --> 14:36.230
Man, I'm beat.

14:36.980 --> 14:40.520
<i>I really need to find some way 
to return to the real world.</i>

14:46.500 --> 14:48.150
Welcome!

14:49.240 --> 14:51.080
Um, I...

14:51.080 --> 14:54.030
Oh, you must be Hirose Natsuko!

14:54.030 --> 14:55.760
You're the new Nine Soldier, yes?

14:56.160 --> 14:59.830
Wow. That sure was fast.

15:01.740 --> 15:07.510
I'm Naomi. I'm the matron here, 
but I also manage the Heroes' Hall,

15:07.510 --> 15:09.770
so if you ever need anything, let me know.

15:09.770 --> 15:11.140
Here's your milk beer.

15:12.420 --> 15:15.040
This is the milk beer 
I've seen so many times?

15:20.230 --> 15:23.660
It's so good! I thought it'd be grosser!

15:23.660 --> 15:25.030
And here's this.

15:26.040 --> 15:28.650
You've gotta eat your cutlets
 before a battle.

15:28.650 --> 15:31.040
'Cause then you can <i>cut</i> down those Voids!

15:31.040 --> 15:32.140
Just kidding!

15:32.140 --> 15:35.350
I hear you use some 
amazing summoning magic.

15:32.520 --> 15:36.000
<i>This rando character reminds me of someone.</i>

15:35.350 --> 15:38.090
You just keep taking down
 those Voids for us!

15:37.150 --> 15:38.380
<i>Naomi?</i>

15:38.380 --> 15:41.140
Oh, pardon moi.

15:41.140 --> 15:42.570
Forgive me, mmkay?

15:43.590 --> 15:44.650
<i>It's the president!</i>

15:44.650 --> 15:46.330
Eat it, mmkay?

15:46.330 --> 15:48.590
<i>"Naomi" is the president's name.</i>

15:48.590 --> 15:49.910
Well, enjoy your stay.

15:48.590 --> 15:51.850
<i>Oh, and I guess she was 
a producer on </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>.</i>

15:52.380 --> 15:55.930
<i>I wonder if the president knew she ended
 up as a background character in this.</i>

15:56.570 --> 16:02.960
<i>Wait, if people from the real world are here, 
I wonder if there's some connection to it.</i>

16:02.960 --> 16:05.220
<i>Maybe there's a hint or 
something on getting back.</i>

16:08.180 --> 16:09.660
<i>The real world...</i>

16:10.420 --> 16:11.920
<i>Do I want to go back?</i>

16:14.300 --> 16:15.750
Hurry it up!

16:15.750 --> 16:18.230
We're gonna finish this up today!

16:22.530 --> 16:23.440
They're here.

16:27.930 --> 16:29.880
They actually came.

16:30.560 --> 16:33.190
Memerun. Unio. Look after the city.

16:33.190 --> 16:34.100
Understood.

16:34.100 --> 16:35.270
Good luck, everyone!

16:35.990 --> 16:37.760
You're over here.

16:41.760 --> 16:43.260
H-Hey!

16:44.330 --> 16:45.650
Use your summoning magic.

16:46.260 --> 16:47.950
I told you, I can't.

16:47.950 --> 16:49.450
Voids confirmed!

16:54.820 --> 16:56.360
Uh, this looks pretty bad.

16:56.360 --> 17:02.200
The probability of Luke being able 
to defeat them on his own is only 3%.

17:02.200 --> 17:04.320
See? Let's hurry up and run!

17:04.320 --> 17:06.690
If we run away, 
who's going to protect this city?

17:07.280 --> 17:10.290
Fight or die. Choose one.

17:10.290 --> 17:12.210
That's what it means to be a Nine Soldier!

17:14.210 --> 17:15.280
Luke!

17:15.690 --> 17:18.080
Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko.

17:18.080 --> 17:18.960
Is it time?

17:18.960 --> 17:20.160
Draw.

17:21.630 --> 17:23.750
See? You can hear it, right?

17:23.750 --> 17:26.350
No, I can't hear a thing!

17:27.080 --> 17:29.230
Draw. You need to draw.

17:29.230 --> 17:31.620
Please hurry and use your 
summoning spell! Or Luke will...

17:31.620 --> 17:35.300
It's okay. Don't worry. If it's something 
I've drawn before, it'll be easy-peasy.

17:35.300 --> 17:36.880
I can draw that giant again.

17:36.880 --> 17:39.310
C'mon! Hurry up and 
spit out my animation desk!

17:39.310 --> 17:40.750
No stock footage.

17:40.750 --> 17:43.180
You cannot draw the same thing again.

17:43.180 --> 17:44.160
What?!

17:44.160 --> 17:47.240
You cannot draw the same thing.
 Only new things.

17:47.240 --> 17:49.130
You should've said that first!

17:49.130 --> 17:52.140
Natsuko-san, hurry! 
Luke cannot handle them on his own!

17:52.140 --> 17:55.000
A mid-air battle... A mid-air battle...

18:07.970 --> 18:08.940
Fire!

18:27.450 --> 18:30.050
Megi Amideki Magiya!

18:32.790 --> 18:34.100
A mid-air battle...

18:34.100 --> 18:38.090
Mid-air battle, mid-air battle, mid-air battle,
 mid-air battle, mid-air battle...

18:45.250 --> 18:48.190
Hirose Natsuko!

18:49.010 --> 18:50.060
That's it!

19:41.870 --> 19:44.820
Damn. There's no end to them.

19:51.960 --> 19:52.950
Natsuko-san!

19:52.950 --> 19:55.720
We can only hold out 
for about a minute longer!

19:57.080 --> 20:00.650
Natsuko!

20:02.840 --> 20:04.100
It's done!

20:08.080 --> 20:13.410
Go!

21:03.400 --> 21:06.040
That black-haired gremlin actually did it.

21:15.950 --> 21:18.290
Void response at 0%!

21:18.290 --> 21:19.990
The Voids have been eradicated!

21:21.250 --> 21:23.570
Good work... everyone...

21:45.670 --> 21:48.190
Mm, so good!

21:48.700 --> 21:50.710
Did you make all this yourself, Luke?

21:51.200 --> 21:52.200
Yeah.

21:52.200 --> 21:54.750
I guess I fell asleep for three days again.

21:54.750 --> 21:58.780
I mean, I guess it would take me 
three days to do that key animation.

22:03.980 --> 22:04.960
What?

22:04.960 --> 22:06.730
No, it's nothing.

22:07.110 --> 22:08.740
Here. Eat this, too.

22:11.310 --> 22:12.470
Yummy!

22:14.340 --> 22:15.480
Yum!

22:17.130 --> 22:19.730
So good!

23:49.990 --> 23:54.900
<b>Episode 3: "Destiny."</b>
